<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Blohm &amp; Voss</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1877</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Blohm &amp; Voss is a shipbuilding company founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a> in 1877 by Hermann Blohm and Ernst Voss. It built liners and warships and, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, the battleship Bismarck and many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/u-boat">U-boats</a>, as well as aircraft through a subsidiary. Its yard on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> opposite the city centre remains one of Hamburg's landmarks.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/blohm-voss.jpg" alt="Blohm &amp; Voss" width="320" height="297" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Duke Q · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BlohmPlusVoss.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
